{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-63h4-6cx9-pjfj","cve_id":null,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security-advisories/GHSA-63h4-6cx9-pjfj","html_url":"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/security/advisories/GHSA-63h4-6cx9-pjfj","summary":"Panic viewing component model stream or future as the wrong type","description":"### Summary\r\n\r\nWasmtime may panic if host tries to read from a `StreamReader<T>` which, prior to passing through guest code, was created as a `StreamReader<U>`, where `T` and `U` are different types which both correspond to the same component model type.\r\n\r\n### Details\r\n\r\nIt is possible for an embedder to create a stream using `StreamReader::<T>::new`, pass it to guest code, and receive it again later from guest code as a different type `StreamReader<U>` as long as both `T` and `U` correspond to the same component model type.  In this case, since the host holds both the read- and write-ends of the stream, Wasmtime will attempt to optimize reads by moving the items directly from the source buffer to the destination buffer without any lifting or lowering.  However, in order for that to work, the source and destination item types must match, and this was ensured by comparing the Rust `TypeId`s and panicking if they didn't match.  That should have been an error rather than a panic.\r\n\r\n### Impact\r\n\r\nEmbedder code which creates streams using `StreamReader::new`, passes them to guest code, and accepts streams back from the guest using a different Rust-level item type may be affected.","severity":"medium","author":null,"publisher":{"login":"alexcrichton","id":64996,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0OTk2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64996?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton","html_url":"https://github.com/alexcrichton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alexcrichton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-63h4-6cx9-pjfj","type":"GHSA"}],"state":"published","created_at":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:25:40Z","published_at":"2026-10-14T17:25:39Z","closed_at":null,"withdrawn_at":null,"submission":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"rust","name":"wasmtime"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 46.0.0, < 48.0.6, >= 49.0.0, < 49.0.3","patched_versions":"48.0.6, 49.0.3","vulnerable_functions":[]}],"cvss_severities":{"cvss_v3":{"vector_string":null,"score":null},"cvss_v4":{"vector_string":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","score":5.9}},"cwes":[],"cwe_ids":[],"credits":[{"login":"tschneidereit","type":"reporter"}],"credits_detailed":[{"user":{"login":"tschneidereit","id":56359,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MzU5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56359?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tschneidereit","html_url":"https://github.com/tschneidereit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tschneidereit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tschneidereit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tschneidereit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tschneidereit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tschneidereit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tschneidereit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tschneidereit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tschneidereit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tschneidereit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"type":"reporter","state":"accepted"}],"collaborating_users":null,"collaborating_teams":null,"private_fork":null,"comments":2,"cvss":{"vector_string":null,"score":null}}